Kanban is an engine for <<.graph>> that lays a graph out as a Kanban board. Nodes become cards in columns and swimlanes, decided by fields of their tiddlers, and edges become arrows between the cards.

<$boundingbox width=100% height=560px>

<$graph.view $tiddler="$:/graph/Kanban Demo" />

</$boundingbox>

Try it: drag a card to another column or swimlane and look at its `status` and `owner` fields, hover a column header to rename or move it, or use ''+ Column'' and the ''+'' at the bottom of a cell. To connect two cards, drag the blue dot of a card onto another card; click an arrow to remove it.

! Pros

* A card's column and swimlane are ordinary fields of its tiddler, so filters, lists and other boards see the same status.
* Columns and swimlanes are configurable in the graph settings and right on the board.
* Arrows between cards show which task leads to or blocks which, and are drawn by dragging from card to card, as on the [[Pinboard]].
* No third-party library.

! Cons

* No free placement and no automatic layout; use [[Pinboard]] for that.
* Experimental.

! Installation

Drag this pill onto your wiki along with <<.graph>>:

@@text-align:center;
<$link to="$:/plugins/lasjoh-toho/kanban" class="graph-dragger graph-dragger-engine">{{$:/core/images/list-bullet}}<br>Kanban</$link>
@@

Then pick the template ''Kanban (columns & swimlanes)'' in a graph's settings.

